  "id": "agent_judgment",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "depends_on": [],
  "self_load_only": true,
  "description": "GENERIC decision-by-collapse (block 312000): ANY agent forms its OWN conclusion about a matter and acts on it. An agent that -considers-> a Matter{claim,weight} (-about_subject-> a person) COLLAPSES over the seeded Stance candidates (denounce/condemn/doubt/exonerate, each a signed pole): jc_conclude sets its Conclusion.verdict = Attr(Argmax over Stances valued by -(stance.pole - lean)^2, 'label'), where lean mixes the EVIDENCE (m.weight, as THIS agent weighs it by its own credence), the agent's own disposition (punitiveness; negative=lenient), and who the SUBJECT is (the agent's deference to the subject's standing). Different agents reach DIFFERENT verdicts on the SAME matter because the value Term reads each agent's OWN held params -- the collapse is subjective by construction (set every disposition equal -> everyone lands on one verdict: the built-in falsifier). Then the citizenry ACTS: jc_act -- a condemning conclusion (verdict_pole>0) strips the subject's public standing by that agent's own sanction, once, when the town is armed to act; the accused's standing emerges from the distribution of independent private verdicts. The court is one application (councillors are agents whose aggregated condemnation, past a threshold, carries legal force); the townsfolk are agents whose aggregated condemnation carries social force -- ONE decision mechanism, two consequences.",
